# UI boundaries

## Hard rule A — `packages/ui` never imports `packages/agents`

`@wunderstack/ui` is presentational. Components receive data via props; apps wire agent calls.
Enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`, dependency-cruiser (`no-ui-to-agents`), and
`scripts/check-ui-boundaries.sh`.

## Hard rule B — semantic tokens only in components

Components in `packages/ui` must reference only semantic tokens (`--color-*`, `--state-*`,
`--radius-*`) or their Tailwind semantic utilities (`bg-primary`, `text-state-verified-fg`, etc.).
Never raw hex values or primitive token names (`--indigo-*`, `--neutral-*`) in component files.

Primitive and semantic CSS lives under `packages/ui/src/tokens/`.

## Removability

`apps/playground` is a leaf consumer. Removing it must leave the repo green (only route registration
removed). `apps/runtime` is API-only and does not consume `packages/ui`.
